WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.890 line:-1 align:center size:84%
The dashboard builds itself from any
dataset or SQL query.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.127 line:-1 align:center size:84%
The platform detects the metrics,
the dimensions and the time column,

00:00:10.127 --> 00:00:12.160 line:-1 align:center size:84%
and decides what is worth showing.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.533 line:-1 align:center size:84%
Every indicator compares against the
previous month, against the same

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:23.131 line:-1 align:center size:84%
month last year, and year to date
against the previous one. Green when

00:00:23.131 --> 00:00:24.970 line:-1 align:center size:84%
it grows, red when it falls.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.597 line:-1 align:center size:84%
And it respects the unit: amounts
vary in percent, and what already is

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.290 line:-1 align:center size:84%
a percentage varies in percentage
points.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.850 line:-1 align:center size:84%
Filters recalculate everything:
indicators, series, bars and table.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.870 line:-1 align:center size:84%
The whole dashboard exports to Excel
or CSV with the filters applied, one

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.270 line:-1 align:center size:84%
sheet per chart.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.854 line:-1 align:center size:84%
And you can ask it in plain
language. It translates the question

00:00:49.854 --> 00:00:52.600 line:-1 align:center size:84%
into SQL, actually runs it against
the data and answers from the real

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.000 line:-1 align:center size:84%
result, not from memory.
